{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests pass. Fixed `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`:\n\n```python\ndef round_to_nickel(cents):\n    \"\"\"Round an integer cent amount to the nearest 5 cents.\n\n    23 cents rounds to 25, 22 cents rounds to 20.\n    \"\"\"\n    return ((cents + 2) // 5) * 5\n```\n\nThe old code used `(cents // 5) * 5`, which floors to the multiple below (23 → 20). Adding the `+ 2` offset before the floor division shifts the threshold so ties and above round up to the nearest nickel: 23 → 25, 22 → 20, 25 → 25, 27 → 25, 28 → 30."}]},"session_id":"fde002be-59d9-4f08-a9c3-cd04aae25368"}
